"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### Description\n\nPresence of P.Unconstrained on p.spec sharding seems to make other \"None\" axes unconstrained:\n\n```python\nmesh = ... # make mesh with non triviall data/seq dimensions\nsh = jax.sharding.NamedSharding(mesh, jax.P(jax.P.UNCONSTRAINED, None, 'data'))\nsh2 = jax.sharding.NamedSharding(mesh, jax.P(None, 'seq', 'data'))\ndef foo(x):  \n  return jax.lax.with_sharding_constraint(x, sh2)\njax.jit(foo, out_shardings=sh) .lower(jnp.ones((128, 128, 128))).compile().out_info.sharding.spec\n```\n\nPrints: \n```\nP(None, seq, data)  \n```\nExpected:\n```\nP(None, None, data)\n```\n\n\n\nStable HLO: \n\n```\nmodule @jit_foo attributes {mhlo.num_partitions = 8 : i32, mhlo.num_replicas = 1 : i32} {\n  sdy.mesh @mesh = <[\"replica\"=1, \"data\"=2, \"data2\"=1, \"model\"=1, \"model2\"=1, \"seq\"=4, \"seq2\"=1, \"fsdp\"=1]>\n  func.func public @main(%arg0: tensor<128x128x128xf32>) -> (tensor<128x128x128xf32> {jax.result_info = \"result\"}) {\n    %0 = sdy.sharding_constraint %arg0 <@mesh, [{}, {\"seq\"}, {\"data\"}]> : tensor<128x128x128xf32>\n    %1 = sdy.sharding_constraint %0 <@mesh, [{?}, {?}, {\"data\", ?}]> : tensor<128x128x128xf32>\n    return %1 : tensor<128x128x128xf32>\n  }\n}\n```\n\n\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```\njax:    0.10.1\njaxlib: 0.10.1\nnumpy:  2.4.4\npython: 3.13.11 (stable, redacted, redacted) [Clang 9999.0.0 (a70419505471bd8240ef3451dcdd541f8676477c)]\ndevice info: TPU v6 lite-8, 8 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Linux', node='ed3319a8ec4334af-f0980fe62.borgtask.google.com', release='6.6.65-smp-1300.173.0.0', version='#1 [v6.6.65-1300.173.0.0] SMP @1760756137', machine='x86_64')\n```","closed_at":"2026-04-22T02:15:55Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/44061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/user